<title>MEXICO: Mexican crude port Dos Bocas reopens.</title>
<headline>Mexican crude port Dos Bocas reopens.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Mexican crude port Dos Bocas in Tabasco state reopened at 1200 local/1800 GMT on Wednesday after a three-day closure as wind speeds relaxed, port officials said.</p>
<p>Dos Bocas is the last of Mexico's three main crude shipping ports to open after a storm hit the Gulf of Mexico earlier this week. The port was shut for three days amid winds as high as 75 km per hour and waves of up to 14 feet high.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
</text>
